//
// Lenovo's real mediatek-common.jar (88 KB, dex contains com.mediatek.common.*
// including IMtkGeofence$Stub, MtkPackageManager hooks, etc.) declared as a
// Soong dex_import so it can participate in PRODUCT_BOOT_JARS.
//
// Why a duplicate copy of the jar in device tree instead of pointing dex_import
// at vendor/lenovo/TB375FC/proprietary/...:  vendor/lenovo/TB375FC/Android.bp
// is auto-generated by tools/gen_vendor_mk.py (which opens it with 'w' mode and
// truncates every entry on each run). Putting the dex_import there would get
// wiped on the next gen-script run. The device tree is hand-maintained, so the
// copy here is the stable home. Same pattern as gf_tee.ko and
// wlan_drv_gen4m_6897.ko prebuilts/modules/vendor_dlkm/.
//
// Why not just leave mediatek-common as the LOS-source 2 KB stub at
// hardware/mediatek/frameworks/common/Android.bp:  the LOS stub's classes.dex
// is essentially empty (1712 bytes vs 88,328 bytes here). hardware/mediatek/
// frameworks/mediatek-frameworks.mk adds `mediatek-common` to PRODUCT_BOOT_JARS,
// and Soong resolves that to the LOS stub install path
// (/system/framework/mediatek-common.jar). Vendor MTK apps -- MtkGeofence
// (com.mediatek.location.mtkgeofence), MtkSettingsProvider, callrecorder etc.
// -- ClassNotFound-crash at runtime because IMtkGeofence$Stub and friends are
// in the proprietary jar at /system_ext/framework/mediatek-common.jar that
// isn't in BOOTCLASSPATH.
//
// Override mechanism: declare this dex_import with the SAME NAME as the LOS
// source's `mediatek-common` module and set `prefer: true`. Soong's prebuilt-
// vs-source resolution picks this prebuilt; the LOS java_library at
// hardware/mediatek/frameworks/common/Android.bp becomes inactive (not built,
// not installed, not in BOOTCLASSPATH). This avoids the hiddenapi class-
// duplication error that occurs when both modules end up in the boot dex set.
// Soong's `prefer: true` is the documented pattern for replacing a source
// module with a prebuilt across the build (build/soong/java/dex_import.go).

dex_import {
    name: "mediatek-common",
    owner: "lenovo",
    jars: ["mediatek-common.jar"],
    prefer: true,
}
